7a86a93725.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[-2,3].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $-1$ and $1$ inclusively, then there exists a number $\\text{ ________ }$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-2,3]$, the intermediate value theorem states that \n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $f(-2)$ and $f(3)$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [-2,3]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nFrom the graph we see that $f(-2)=1$ and $f(3)=-1.$Therefore, the missing part is \"$c\\in [-2,3]$\"\n\n![](images/85/85a590ba283dae96329692fee1aa6e08045fb06e5baa8a42d8308fe8c2558f02.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3259bb32-160b-584a-9d3c-ccfd3a1756c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3259bb32-160b-584a-9d3c-ccfd3a1756c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "3259bb32-160b-584a-9d3c-ccfd3a1756c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2cb9c562-97a9-59a7-9eae-91d8984e88a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b37e21ab-0f08-5606-90dc-a04d243f4e4f" "answer-93a5119a-6a61-5673-8be7-e0b3955b04c1" "answer-eb407e1a-f60c-5528-b589-8ea53f4c6814" "answer-1d232c74-e493-5e95-b19e-bef59d74487c" "answer-2cb9c562-97a9-59a7-9eae-91d8984e88a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b37e21ab-0f08-5606-90dc-a04d243f4e4f" :answer/id #uuid "b37e21ab-0f08-5606-90dc-a04d243f4e4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c\\in (-1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93a5119a-6a61-5673-8be7-e0b3955b04c1" :answer/id #uuid "93a5119a-6a61-5673-8be7-e0b3955b04c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c\\in (-2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb407e1a-f60c-5528-b589-8ea53f4c6814" :answer/id #uuid "eb407e1a-f60c-5528-b589-8ea53f4c6814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c\\in [-1,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d232c74-e493-5e95-b19e-bef59d74487c" :answer/id #uuid "1d232c74-e493-5e95-b19e-bef59d74487c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c\\in [-2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cb9c562-97a9-59a7-9eae-91d8984e88a7" :answer/id #uuid "2cb9c562-97a9-59a7-9eae-91d8984e88a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c\\in [-2,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134476 :question/problem "A statement of the intermediate value theorem is given below but some of its parts are missing.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is $\\text{ ______ }$ on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ _________ }$, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nGoing from left to right, in which order should the parts I-III listed below be placed into the blank spaces to complete the statement of the theorem?\n\nI. increasing\n\nII. continuous\n\nIII. $f(a)$ and $f(b)$ inclusively" :question/worked-solution "The intermediate value theorem states the following.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is **continuous** on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $f(a)$ **and** $f(b)$ **inclusively**, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II, III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186132894 :answer-field/correct 17592186132895 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-649e731a-c63d-5be5-bf6d-a7054ad65b37" :question/id #uuid "649e731a-c63d-5be5-bf6d-a7054ad65b37" :question/math-academy-id "q-48342" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-\\sqrt{x}$ which is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[0,4].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ ________ }$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [0,4]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,4],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(0)$ and $f(4).$\n\nSince $f(0)=0$ and $f(4)=14$, we must have \n$k\\in [0,14].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$0$ and $14$\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-523da1f1-a357-58c6-b31e-b24677539075"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-523da1f1-a357-58c6-b31e-b24677539075" :answer-field/id #uuid "523da1f1-a357-58c6-b31e-b24677539075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95ef29c0-8c06-5acf-9af0-bffc2f268169" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1aa6b76-69df-564d-b084-f23ee24ba4b4" "answer-73456ba9-56d5-5c2f-9bb3-0f255baaa1c7" "answer-95ef29c0-8c06-5acf-9af0-bffc2f268169" "answer-b4c42683-7d2e-56d1-aab0-70703cd960e3" "answer-e4c6c514-c088-5630-96e3-d9f2191a0659"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1aa6b76-69df-564d-b084-f23ee24ba4b4" :answer/id #uuid "f1aa6b76-69df-564d-b084-f23ee24ba4b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4$ and $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73456ba9-56d5-5c2f-9bb3-0f255baaa1c7" :answer/id #uuid "73456ba9-56d5-5c2f-9bb3-0f255baaa1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95ef29c0-8c06-5acf-9af0-bffc2f268169" :answer/id #uuid "95ef29c0-8c06-5acf-9af0-bffc2f268169" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $14$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c42683-7d2e-56d1-aab0-70703cd960e3" :answer/id #uuid "b4c42683-7d2e-56d1-aab0-70703cd960e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $16$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4c6c514-c088-5630-96e3-d9f2191a0659" :answer/id #uuid "e4c6c514-c088-5630-96e3-d9f2191a0659" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-60c91108-e44c-5a52-8d9f-b008dcd257b3" :question/id #uuid "60c91108-e44c-5a52-8d9f-b008dcd257b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105621" :question/problem "![](images/87/87bcea590bfb7357728d64cadabf4ab3e85135d312a60dd092ec546727a5fa30.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[-1,4].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ ________ }$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [-1,4]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,4],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-1)$ and $f(4)$ inclusively.\n\nSince $f(-1)=5$ and $f(4)=-1$, we must have \n$k\\in [-1,5].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$-1$ and $5$\".\n\n![](images/1c/1c823d5f99ac9a126d3144197a493f347df20215c30b5ee7b28dc136459f00a2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31715bc6-dcf3-5721-ab14-4c1ca08aad86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31715bc6-dcf3-5721-ab14-4c1ca08aad86" :answer-field/id #uuid "31715bc6-dcf3-5721-ab14-4c1ca08aad86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b304347-eeba-582b-acf5-04fc708bf3c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-baa9601c-c987-51b0-8c57-a0a53c1b38c4" "answer-0b304347-eeba-582b-acf5-04fc708bf3c6" "answer-c9dda439-ccd3-5069-8f04-60636b0d51d3" "answer-7808b15c-0db4-598e-9af1-b4b030735c09" "answer-9a4f05e6-1064-5237-8152-301e601e93a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baa9601c-c987-51b0-8c57-a0a53c1b38c4" :answer/id #uuid "baa9601c-c987-51b0-8c57-a0a5